# Smart Parking System Algorithm

## 1. Setup

N = total number of slots in the lot
availableSlots = min-heap containing slot ids {1, 2, ..., N}
activeTickets = hash map: vehiclePlate -> Ticket{slotId, entryTime, vehicleType}
rateTable = hash map: vehicleType -> (firstHourRate, extraHourRate)


## 2. Check Availability (before entry)

FUNCTION checkAvailability():
freeCount = size(availableSlots)
RETURN (freeCount > 0, freeCount)

Cost: O(1). This is what a display board or mobile app polls continuously.

## 3. Vehicle Entry

FUNCTION vehicleEntry(plate, vehicleType):
IF activeTickets.contains(plate):
RETURN ERROR "Vehicle already parked"

IF isEmpty(availableSlots):
    RETURN ERROR "Parking Full"

slotId    = heap_pop_min(availableSlots)      # lowest free slot, O(log N)
entryTime = now()
ticket    = Ticket(plate, slotId, entryTime, vehicleType)

activeTickets.put(plate, ticket)               # O(1)
DB.insert(vehicle, slot_status=OCCUPIED, transaction row with entry_time)

RETURN ticket   # tells the driver which slot to go to

## 4. Vehicle Exit

FUNCTION vehicleExit(plate):
IF NOT activeTickets.contains(plate):
RETURN ERROR "Ticket not found"

ticket    = activeTickets.remove(plate)         # O(1)
exitTime  = now()
duration  = exitTime - ticket.entryTime          # in seconds
hours     = CEIL(duration / 3600)                # partial hour billed as full hour
fee       = computeFee(ticket.vehicleType, hours)

heap_push(availableSlots, ticket.slotId)         # slot is free again, O(log N)
DB.update(transaction row: exit_time, duration, amount_paid = fee)
DB.update(slot: status = FREE)

RETURN (duration, fee)

FUNCTION computeFee(vehicleType, hours):
(firstHourRate, extraHourRate) = rateTable[vehicleType]
IF hours <= 1:
RETURN firstHourRate
RETURN firstHourRate + (hours - 1) * extraHourRate


## 5. Complexity Summary
| Operation            | Time Complexity |
|-----------------------|------------------|
| Check availability    | O(1) |
| Vehicle entry          | O(log N)  heap pop |
| Vehicle exit           | O(log N)  heap push, O(1) lookup |
| Fee calculation        | O(1) |

`N` = number of slots, so even a 10,000-slot facility responds in microseconds.